1
00:00:00,031 --> 00:00:01,495
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,497 --> 00:00:03,000
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,163 --> 00:00:05,266
(Episode 66)

4
00:00:05,291 --> 00:00:07,499
Are you really feeling okay?

5
00:00:08,779 --> 00:00:10,422
Do you remember everything?

6
00:00:12,384 --> 00:00:13,605
Who am I?

7
00:00:17,331 --> 00:00:18,595
You're the woman I love...

8
00:00:20,125 --> 00:00:21,354
Ji Ni.

9
00:00:24,179 --> 00:00:26,200
Are your memories really back?

10
00:00:27,465 --> 00:00:29,006
You remember everything, right?

11
00:00:30,423 --> 00:00:31,425
I'm sorry.

12
00:00:32,412 --> 00:00:35,380
You must've suffered so much
because I was such a fool.

13
00:00:36,132 --> 00:00:37,403
Let's go to the hospital now.

14
00:00:37,759 --> 00:00:38,806
Let's make sure.

15
00:00:39,538 --> 00:00:41,116
Remembering you is all I need.

16
00:00:42,545 --> 00:00:44,763
The other memories can come back slowly.

17
00:00:49,212 --> 00:00:50,648
I thought you might...

18
00:00:51,699 --> 00:00:54,659
go back to England without remembering me.

19
00:00:56,465 --> 00:00:57,924
I was so scared.

20
00:00:58,322 --> 00:00:59,638
And I had so many regrets.

21
00:01:01,939 --> 00:01:04,696
When you coldly told me on the phone...

22
00:01:06,321 --> 00:01:08,518
"This is the end,"

23
00:01:10,262 --> 00:01:12,392
I felt like my world was falling apart.

24
00:01:17,245 --> 00:01:19,037
I've changed a lot, right?

25
00:01:21,238 --> 00:01:23,224
Hearing you say that...

26
00:01:24,235 --> 00:01:26,315
I can't tell if this is real or a dream.

27
00:01:30,972 --> 00:01:32,053
Let's go outside.

28
00:01:32,370 --> 00:01:33,692
I need some fresh air.

29
00:01:40,883 --> 00:01:42,416
(Your marriage has been registered.
Congratulations.)

30
00:01:42,418 --> 00:01:43,742
(Civil Affairs Division,
Seongbok District Office, Seoul)

31
00:01:59,071 --> 00:02:01,039
Aren't you going home, Tae O?

32
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:04,495
It's that late already?

33
00:02:05,091 --> 00:02:06,414
You can leave first.

34
00:02:06,577 --> 00:02:08,540
I've been away so long.
There's a lot to do.

35
00:02:09,785 --> 00:02:11,104
I'll head out, then.

36
00:02:11,641 --> 00:02:13,349
I'll head out too.

37
00:02:25,745 --> 00:02:27,440
Ji Hu remembers me.

38
00:02:27,465 --> 00:02:29,212
We're going for a walk.

39
00:02:38,718 --> 00:02:40,889
I'm so glad. That's great news.

40
00:02:41,304 --> 00:02:43,327
Take time to talk and enjoy yourselves.

41
00:02:52,558 --> 00:02:53,721
Hello?

42
00:02:55,202 --> 00:02:56,202
Something up?

43
00:02:56,833 --> 00:02:58,308
There is, actually.

44
00:02:58,332 --> 00:02:59,951
Have you closed the cafe?

45
00:02:59,975 --> 00:03:01,184
Want a late-night snack?

46
00:03:02,691 --> 00:03:05,083
Never mind. If you're busy, it's okay.

47
00:03:05,634 --> 00:03:06,634
Bye.

48
00:03:42,798 --> 00:03:44,438
Why did you jump in front of that car?

49
00:03:44,463 --> 00:03:46,116
What if you'd actually died?

50
00:03:50,945 --> 00:03:53,866
I'd have been glad
if it had been me instead of you.

51
00:03:53,948 --> 00:03:55,022
That's nonsense.

52
00:03:55,226 --> 00:03:56,867
Don't say something so awful.

53
00:03:56,892 --> 00:03:58,980
Were you really that afraid I'd die?

54
00:04:01,385 --> 00:04:03,373
How many times do I have to tell you?

55
00:04:04,592 --> 00:04:06,290
I just love hearing you say it.

56
00:04:06,644 --> 00:04:09,445
You hit me right here
when I told you about my feelings.

57
00:04:10,058 --> 00:04:11,465
I was so devastated.

58
00:04:16,264 --> 00:04:18,392
I told you
not to put me in this situation.

59
00:04:18,666 --> 00:04:20,348
I said I didn't want this!

60
00:04:24,878 --> 00:04:26,605
I really regretted it.

61
00:04:27,011 --> 00:04:28,057
I'm sorry.

62
00:04:35,025 --> 00:04:36,152
Actually, I...

63
00:04:36,793 --> 00:04:39,002
met my birth mother
when I was in high school.

64
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:40,275
Really?

65
00:04:41,218 --> 00:04:42,267
At the time...

66
00:04:42,804 --> 00:04:44,027
I asked why she'd shown up.

67
00:04:44,051 --> 00:04:46,378
Why look for me now after abandoning me?

68
00:04:46,896 --> 00:04:48,097
I was furious with her.

69
00:04:50,025 --> 00:04:53,478
Growing up, I didn't feel
very loved by my adoptive mom.

70
00:04:55,197 --> 00:04:58,498
I was always lonely and longing for love.

71
00:05:00,211 --> 00:05:03,218
I thought being abandoned was why
I felt that way. I was young...

72
00:05:03,698 --> 00:05:04,972
and it made me furious.

73
00:05:06,225 --> 00:05:07,801
Of course you felt that way.

74
00:05:08,292 --> 00:05:10,341
Then I found the courage to meet her.

75
00:05:11,892 --> 00:05:13,328
I hoped she'd had a reason...

76
00:05:13,353 --> 00:05:15,748
that she'd had to give me up
rather than just abandon me.

77
00:05:17,744 --> 00:05:19,176
But she didn't show up.

78
00:05:20,818 --> 00:05:23,663
She was the one who wanted to meet,
yet I was abandoned again.

79
00:05:24,557 --> 00:05:26,712
So that's why you reacted that way...

80
00:05:26,737 --> 00:05:28,609
when I couldn't make it to our meeting.

81
00:05:30,052 --> 00:05:33,770
I got my hopes up,
thinking we'd meet again,

82
00:05:34,329 --> 00:05:36,253
but I was left devastated.

83
00:05:39,252 --> 00:05:40,925
After that, I got wrist tendinitis...

84
00:05:41,667 --> 00:05:43,168
and went back to England.

85
00:05:44,533 --> 00:05:45,685
I regretted it.

86
00:05:47,211 --> 00:05:49,157
I should've arranged to meet her again.

87
00:05:49,341 --> 00:05:51,763
I still had questions.
Why couldn't I ask to see her again?

88
00:05:55,974 --> 00:05:58,490
If I'd left for England this time
without regaining my memory,

89
00:05:59,234 --> 00:06:00,749
I'd have regretted it again.

90
00:06:02,859 --> 00:06:04,750
I'd have wished I'd seen you again.

91
00:06:07,731 --> 00:06:09,353
I'm so glad.

92
00:06:10,122 --> 00:06:12,873
I've been given another chance.

93
00:06:15,005 --> 00:06:17,782
I'd finally found the courage
to stop running from love,

94
00:06:17,940 --> 00:06:20,125
but then I couldn't see you.

95
00:06:21,393 --> 00:06:23,486
I thought, "I'm so unlucky."

96
00:06:24,186 --> 00:06:25,997
I felt so hopeless.

97
00:06:33,698 --> 00:06:36,386
So today's our first day together, right?

98
00:07:10,201 --> 00:07:11,325
Get home safely.

99
00:07:11,465 --> 00:07:12,807
I'll wait until you go in.

100
00:07:14,198 --> 00:07:16,556
I'll go in once I turn around.

101
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:17,682
You go first.

102
00:07:18,192 --> 00:07:20,366
Let's turn around together
on the count of three.

103
00:07:20,945 --> 00:07:22,968
One, two, three!

104
00:07:22,999 --> 00:07:25,213
Three. Get lost.

105
00:07:25,827 --> 00:07:27,770
- Mom...
- What's going on?

106
00:07:27,795 --> 00:07:29,299
What are you two doing out here?

107
00:07:29,412 --> 00:07:31,431
You're going to England, right? Go.

108
00:07:34,489 --> 00:07:35,743
Hello, Mother.

109
00:07:36,247 --> 00:07:37,299
Mother?

110
00:07:37,552 --> 00:07:39,133
Since when are we that close?

111
00:07:39,151 --> 00:07:41,021
You barely know him either.
Why glare at him?

112
00:07:42,451 --> 00:07:44,227
Ji Hu, you'd better go.

113
00:07:45,782 --> 00:07:47,661
I'll come visit you another time, then.

114
00:07:47,662 --> 00:07:49,004
No. Don't come.

115
00:07:49,029 --> 00:07:50,848
- I don't want to see you.
- Mom.

116
00:07:51,287 --> 00:07:52,307
What?

117
00:07:52,332 --> 00:07:54,398
Can't I say how I feel?

118
00:07:55,570 --> 00:07:56,676
You should go.

119
00:07:58,739 --> 00:08:01,806
I'm sorry I've worried you so much.

120
00:08:02,158 --> 00:08:03,733
I won't make you worry anymore.

121
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:05,577
Enough. Just go.

122
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:08,381
Goodbye.

123
00:08:16,945 --> 00:08:20,337
I gave you such a pretty face,

124
00:08:20,361 --> 00:08:21,785
and you use it to glare at me?

125
00:08:22,053 --> 00:08:23,397
I take after dad, actually.

126
00:08:26,057 --> 00:08:27,057
Honestly.

127
00:08:33,018 --> 00:08:34,907
What is going on?

128
00:08:34,932 --> 00:08:36,633
Why are you two together?

129
00:08:38,346 --> 00:08:39,989
- Na Ji Ni.
- Mom.

130
00:08:42,465 --> 00:08:44,514
Ji Hu remembers everything now.

131
00:08:44,821 --> 00:08:46,276
Isn't that great?

132
00:08:49,032 --> 00:08:51,155
- Are you that happy?
- Why wouldn't I be?

133
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:53,134
I prayed so hard for this.

134
00:08:53,532 --> 00:08:55,086
We won't be apart anymore.

135
00:08:55,732 --> 00:08:57,328
Can't you see anything but Ji Hu?

136
00:08:58,145 --> 00:08:59,379
What more do I need to see?

137
00:08:59,404 --> 00:09:02,685
What about his parents and Do Do Hee?

138
00:09:02,709 --> 00:09:04,193
Can't you see them too?

139
00:09:04,352 --> 00:09:06,386
They'll destroy you.

140
00:09:06,559 --> 00:09:08,937
Ji Hu and I will win. We have each other.

141
00:09:09,399 --> 00:09:11,789
You and dad overcame everything too.

142
00:09:11,813 --> 00:09:12,889
Overcame?

143
00:09:13,073 --> 00:09:15,737
You're still being insulted
for being my daughter.

144
00:09:16,511 --> 00:09:17,865
So what?

145
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:19,329
Can't you just be happy for me?

146
00:09:19,570 --> 00:09:22,630
"That's wonderful. I'll support you."
Can't you just say that?

147
00:09:22,655 --> 00:09:25,329
Be realistic about what you're facing.

148
00:09:25,331 --> 00:09:26,919
Is this really the time for that?

149
00:09:27,037 --> 00:09:28,186
Get out, Mom.

150
00:09:28,368 --> 00:09:31,868
I said I wouldn't talk to you,
but I let my guard down again.

151
00:09:32,048 --> 00:09:34,300
Come to your senses, you foolish girl.

152
00:09:34,325 --> 00:09:37,180
Find someone normal to love
and have a normal relationship.

153
00:09:37,205 --> 00:09:39,462
Then you should've had me
under normal circumstances.

154
00:09:40,307 --> 00:09:41,393
Ji Ni.

155
00:09:41,445 --> 00:09:43,251
You said something hurtful first, Mom.

156
00:09:43,276 --> 00:09:46,723
They'd let the criminal who tried
to run you over marry their son,

157
00:09:46,724 --> 00:09:48,794
but they reject you for being my daughter.

158
00:09:49,024 --> 00:09:51,424
How can I cheer you on
and congratulate you?

159
00:09:51,441 --> 00:09:53,478
There's nothing but hardship ahead.

160
00:09:56,251 --> 00:09:58,927
Your dad and I wanted...

161
00:09:59,189 --> 00:10:02,463
nothing but an easy life for you.
We wished and begged for it.

162
00:10:03,021 --> 00:10:04,964
Get out.

163
00:10:04,989 --> 00:10:06,117
Stop talking.

164
00:10:06,119 --> 00:10:08,269
I just can't talk to you, Mom.

165
00:10:09,098 --> 00:10:10,596
Honestly!

166
00:10:11,324 --> 00:10:12,890
You little brat.

167
00:10:12,915 --> 00:10:14,864
What a temper.

168
00:10:14,866 --> 00:10:17,072
Where on earth does she get it?

169
00:10:17,097 --> 00:10:19,392
It's so frustrating.

170
00:10:19,417 --> 00:10:23,628
She's more like a bomb than a daughter.
Touch her, and she blows up.

171
00:10:25,183 --> 00:10:26,757
What is it now?

172
00:10:31,838 --> 00:10:33,464
Ji Hu came by?

173
00:10:36,564 --> 00:10:38,430
He got his memory back.

174
00:10:38,657 --> 00:10:40,107
The two of them
were right outside the house,

175
00:10:40,131 --> 00:10:42,376
holding hands like this.

176
00:10:43,294 --> 00:10:44,393
Really?

177
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:46,547
What's with you? Don't get your hopes up.

178
00:10:46,572 --> 00:10:49,402
I'm the one who hoped
he'd never get his memory back.

179
00:10:49,572 --> 00:10:50,880
Even so,

180
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:53,466
Ji Ni has every right to be upset
when she hears you say that.

181
00:10:53,491 --> 00:10:57,876
Losing his memory is better for him
and for our family.

182
00:10:57,972 --> 00:11:01,624
The world's chaotic enough.
We don't need to remember everything.

183
00:11:01,812 --> 00:11:04,109
And even his own family says...

184
00:11:04,133 --> 00:11:07,430
they'd rather have a murderer
as a daughter-in-law than Ji Ni.

185
00:11:08,114 --> 00:11:10,203
If those memories come back,

186
00:11:10,205 --> 00:11:13,207
I'm scared something will happen to Ji Ni.

187
00:11:13,285 --> 00:11:14,976
Still, you shouldn't say that.

188
00:11:15,197 --> 00:11:17,341
You think I'd say this
if I had any other choice?

189
00:11:17,985 --> 00:11:20,989
Please talk to her for me.

190
00:11:21,438 --> 00:11:24,291
She likes you all more than she likes me.

191
00:11:24,316 --> 00:11:26,272
That's ridiculous. You're her mom.

192
00:11:26,297 --> 00:11:29,149
You're so naive.

193
00:11:29,831 --> 00:11:33,582
I'm her mom, but this is all my fault.

194
00:11:33,751 --> 00:11:37,119
Because of me,
she isn't even treated like a human being.

195
00:11:37,418 --> 00:11:39,692
She'll waste away
if she goes to that house.

196
00:11:39,717 --> 00:11:44,000
I understand what you mean,
but please don't worry so much.

197
00:11:44,452 --> 00:11:48,313
They're not getting married tomorrow.
They've only just started dating.

198
00:11:49,087 --> 00:11:51,040
She's such a handful.

199
00:11:59,025 --> 00:12:00,314
I mean it.

200
00:12:00,886 --> 00:12:03,269
I want Ji Ni to have
a beautiful love story.

201
00:12:03,723 --> 00:12:04,943
I'll support you.

202
00:12:10,078 --> 00:12:13,518
Should we just burn Ji Hu's passport?

203
00:12:13,719 --> 00:12:14,720
Then he can't board the plane.

204
00:12:14,745 --> 00:12:16,284
I thought of that too.

205
00:12:16,462 --> 00:12:18,372
But instead of burning it,
we could steal it.

206
00:12:18,397 --> 00:12:19,584
Ji Hu isn't back yet, right?

207
00:12:19,992 --> 00:12:21,690
I'll go steal it right now.

208
00:12:30,292 --> 00:12:31,671
Were you going to burn my passport?

209
00:12:31,938 --> 00:12:34,983
That's not what we were going to do...

210
00:12:38,178 --> 00:12:39,178
What?

211
00:12:42,985 --> 00:12:44,029
Ji Hu...

212
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:46,123
Did you...

213
00:12:47,139 --> 00:12:48,139
Yes.

214
00:12:48,902 --> 00:12:50,910
I'm sorry I made you worry.

215
00:12:51,605 --> 00:12:52,826
I'm not going to England.

216
00:12:52,850 --> 00:12:53,892
Ji Hu, you...

217
00:12:54,612 --> 00:12:56,065
You little rascal!

218
00:13:03,547 --> 00:13:04,895
It's really Ji Hu.

219
00:13:05,427 --> 00:13:07,229
He's finally himself again.

220
00:13:07,478 --> 00:13:09,201
Yes, it's really me.

221
00:13:11,118 --> 00:13:13,680
Hey, come sit down.

222
00:13:15,736 --> 00:13:18,152
Tell us. How did you remember?

223
00:13:18,177 --> 00:13:20,090
It's all thanks...

224
00:13:20,299 --> 00:13:22,994
to the screeching and banging sounds
I played every morning, right?

225
00:13:24,451 --> 00:13:26,025
I don't think that was it.

226
00:13:26,985 --> 00:13:29,834
- The morning music you played helped.
- Really?

227
00:13:29,970 --> 00:13:32,421
Great! That's what matters.

228
00:13:32,445 --> 00:13:33,560
Yeong Ju.

229
00:13:34,205 --> 00:13:36,378
What about your parents?

230
00:13:36,979 --> 00:13:39,048
Joong Bin will be happy too.
I'll go tell him...

231
00:13:40,184 --> 00:13:41,588
I'll tell them when the time is right.

232
00:13:41,941 --> 00:13:42,941
What?

233
00:13:43,066 --> 00:13:44,100
Okay.

234
00:13:44,125 --> 00:13:46,487
Things have gotten complicated.
Do you remember?

235
00:13:46,535 --> 00:13:48,462
They think you're going to England.

236
00:13:48,464 --> 00:13:50,078
And that you're marrying Do Hee.

237
00:13:50,112 --> 00:13:51,521
That's why I have a lot to think about.

238
00:13:52,545 --> 00:13:54,899
I want to sort out my thoughts
before I see Do Hee.

239
00:13:55,326 --> 00:13:56,731
Then I'll tell my parents.

240
00:13:57,251 --> 00:14:00,268
I'll tell them myself,
so please don't say anything until then.

241
00:14:00,851 --> 00:14:02,819
Okay. But...

242
00:14:02,991 --> 00:14:04,000
what about Ji Ni?

243
00:14:04,107 --> 00:14:05,380
Does she know?

244
00:14:05,832 --> 00:14:07,499
I was with Ji Ni.

245
00:14:07,812 --> 00:14:09,739
She helped me get my memory back.

246
00:14:09,992 --> 00:14:11,882
Love really is powerful.

247
00:14:11,985 --> 00:14:13,223
Glad to have you back!

248
00:14:14,492 --> 00:14:17,477
Some people don't regain their memories
for decades.

249
00:14:17,501 --> 00:14:18,714
You're so lucky.

250
00:14:18,739 --> 00:14:20,739
Yes, I'm really grateful to you both.

251
00:14:21,180 --> 00:14:22,786
That shock therapy every morning?

252
00:14:24,432 --> 00:14:26,829
I'll never forget how you kept trying...

253
00:14:26,853 --> 00:14:28,160
to tell me what really happened.

254
00:14:28,845 --> 00:14:30,411
- Get some sleep.
- Okay.

255
00:14:35,584 --> 00:14:38,557
I'm so glad.

256
00:14:39,632 --> 00:14:41,137
Isn't my nephew amazing?

257
00:14:42,004 --> 00:14:44,872
Everyone says he's tall and handsome
just like me.

258
00:14:46,474 --> 00:14:47,687
Yes.

259
00:15:22,605 --> 00:15:24,925
- Yes, Mom.
- Did you register your marriage?

260
00:15:24,994 --> 00:15:26,257
Yeah, I did.

261
00:15:27,145 --> 00:15:29,863
Ji Hu and I are legally married now.

262
00:15:30,552 --> 00:15:32,505
If Na Ji Ni makes a move on him,
she'll be the mistress.

263
00:15:33,152 --> 00:15:35,678
- But he probably won't even look at her.
- Good.

264
00:15:35,865 --> 00:15:37,587
This is a piece of cake.

265
00:15:38,149 --> 00:15:39,149
A recording?

266
00:15:41,125 --> 00:15:43,234
I hadn't even thought of that.

267
00:15:45,145 --> 00:15:46,330
Okay, Mom.

268
00:15:48,718 --> 00:15:50,646
I'll take care of it
and then go to England.

269
00:15:51,389 --> 00:15:52,389
Yeah.

270
00:15:59,052 --> 00:16:00,052
Ji Hu,

271
00:16:00,992 --> 00:16:02,579
we're married now.

272
00:16:03,096 --> 00:16:04,398
You're happy too, right?

273
00:16:18,892 --> 00:16:20,971
Did something good happen last night?

274
00:16:21,005 --> 00:16:22,026
Did you have a nice dream?

275
00:16:22,540 --> 00:16:24,240
What? No, nothing.

276
00:16:24,605 --> 00:16:27,974
I'm just excited to have breakfast
with everyone.

277
00:16:28,937 --> 00:16:30,305
It's not like it's the first time.

278
00:16:32,785 --> 00:16:35,452
Good morning, Mother.

279
00:16:35,453 --> 00:16:37,615
You're here? You're up early.

280
00:16:38,232 --> 00:16:40,558
Isn't it a little early
to visit someone else's home?

281
00:16:40,559 --> 00:16:43,163
Someone else's home?
This is Do Hee's home.

282
00:16:43,165 --> 00:16:44,802
I invited her to breakfast.

283
00:16:44,985 --> 00:16:46,765
We won't see each other much
once they go to England.

284
00:16:47,892 --> 00:16:49,251
That's why I came.

285
00:16:49,297 --> 00:16:50,460
- Mother.
- Yeah?

286
00:16:50,469 --> 00:16:52,377
There's something
I'd like to discuss with you.

287
00:16:52,866 --> 00:16:53,866
Really?

288
00:16:54,032 --> 00:16:55,418
Okay. Let's step outside and talk.

289
00:17:02,452 --> 00:17:04,502
You're finished now, you little brat.

290
00:17:05,319 --> 00:17:06,319
What a relief!

291
00:17:12,151 --> 00:17:13,151
Register your marriage?

292
00:17:13,447 --> 00:17:15,244
He'll get a work visa,

293
00:17:15,418 --> 00:17:17,918
and I can go with him as his spouse.

294
00:17:18,758 --> 00:17:20,463
Now that I'm married,

295
00:17:20,511 --> 00:17:23,237
I can't keep relying on my dad
to protect me forever.

296
00:17:23,605 --> 00:17:25,148
My mom thinks it's a good idea too.

297
00:17:25,455 --> 00:17:26,455
I see.

298
00:17:26,872 --> 00:17:29,659
You've already got things set up
in London. What is there to worry about?

299
00:17:29,964 --> 00:17:30,964
Right?

300
00:17:31,032 --> 00:17:32,918
You and I really are on the same page.

301
00:17:33,085 --> 00:17:34,085
Hey.

302
00:17:34,312 --> 00:17:37,031
We booked the wedding venue last night.

303
00:17:37,192 --> 00:17:39,411
Someone had just canceled,
so we grabbed the spot.

304
00:17:39,413 --> 00:17:42,478
I'm so happy, Mother.

305
00:17:42,948 --> 00:17:45,325
I liked the movie theater
in your husband's building too.

306
00:17:45,327 --> 00:17:47,156
That place is too small.

307
00:17:47,158 --> 00:17:48,705
We have so many guests!

308
00:17:49,238 --> 00:17:51,635
We'll get married soon
and head to England,

309
00:17:51,702 --> 00:17:54,184
then we'll come back
with a grandson and a granddaughter.

310
00:17:55,252 --> 00:17:57,395
You make it sound so easy.

311
00:17:58,705 --> 00:18:01,190
Isn't it easy to have a baby
once I'm married?

312
00:18:01,692 --> 00:18:02,922
I'm still so young.

313
00:18:03,398 --> 00:18:05,585
I used to think life was that easy too.

314
00:18:05,925 --> 00:18:08,504
Mother, was it hard for you to have Ji Hu?

315
00:18:11,025 --> 00:18:12,025
No.

316
00:18:12,746 --> 00:18:13,924
See?

317
00:18:14,052 --> 00:18:15,546
I'll get pregnant in no time too.

318
00:18:38,385 --> 00:18:39,385
What are you doing?

319
00:18:39,422 --> 00:18:40,422
What?

320
00:18:41,093 --> 00:18:43,298
What do you think? Waiting for you.

321
00:18:44,145 --> 00:18:47,047
Ji Hu, your mom picked our wedding venue.

322
00:18:47,498 --> 00:18:50,108
Now that we have a date,
I'll send out digital invitations.

323
00:18:50,611 --> 00:18:52,055
And let's register our marriage.

324
00:18:52,295 --> 00:18:53,911
- Register our marriage?
- Yeah.

325
00:18:54,178 --> 00:18:55,778
Your mom said we should too.

326
00:18:56,656 --> 00:18:58,338
I'm so happy.

327
00:19:00,912 --> 00:19:02,185
Don't do anything just yet.

328
00:19:03,850 --> 00:19:04,850
Why?

329
00:19:05,631 --> 00:19:06,692
I need some time to think.

330
00:19:08,168 --> 00:19:09,972
I'll call you later. Just wait.

331
00:19:11,412 --> 00:19:13,228
What do you need to think about?

332
00:19:14,758 --> 00:19:17,857
What's wrong? It's nothing bad, right?

333
00:19:18,575 --> 00:19:19,575
No.

334
00:19:20,925 --> 00:19:21,925
Ji Hu,

335
00:19:22,669 --> 00:19:24,280
don't change your mind.

336
00:19:25,406 --> 00:19:26,406
Okay?

337
00:19:26,758 --> 00:19:28,568
You're all I have.

338
00:19:34,022 --> 00:19:37,059
- It's true!
- They fit snugly around your feet.

339
00:19:38,546 --> 00:19:41,299
They're perfect for people
who stand for hours.

340
00:19:46,174 --> 00:19:49,511
This is so chaotic. What's going on?

341
00:19:49,591 --> 00:19:51,311
Business is booming!

342
00:19:52,505 --> 00:19:54,178
I came to buy shoes too.

343
00:19:54,232 --> 00:19:55,849
For my son in Jeju.

344
00:19:55,850 --> 00:19:58,336
Recommend something nice and popular.

345
00:19:58,337 --> 00:20:00,018
Really? Well, why not?

346
00:20:00,205 --> 00:20:01,828
Now, what should I pick?

347
00:20:04,215 --> 00:20:05,215
How about these?

348
00:20:07,065 --> 00:20:09,827
You've helped me so much,

349
00:20:09,829 --> 00:20:11,705
so let me buy you a pair this time.

350
00:20:12,171 --> 00:20:15,061
A lot of young people are asking
for these lately.

351
00:20:15,502 --> 00:20:16,502
Take a look.

352
00:20:16,992 --> 00:20:19,212
My son would love these.

353
00:20:19,309 --> 00:20:20,958
They're stylish and simple.

354
00:20:21,092 --> 00:20:23,674
Students who do a lot of walking...

355
00:20:23,675 --> 00:20:25,697
love how comfortable they are.

356
00:20:25,791 --> 00:20:30,116
Parents come in all the time
to buy these for kids studying for exams.

357
00:20:30,118 --> 00:20:31,359
Really?

358
00:20:32,425 --> 00:20:36,219
If they're this good, I'll pay full price.

359
00:20:36,221 --> 00:20:38,007
No, it's fine.

360
00:20:39,344 --> 00:20:40,634
Please ring them up.

361
00:20:41,253 --> 00:20:42,253
Okay, then.

362
00:20:42,438 --> 00:20:45,820
If my son asks for another pair,
you can give me those as a gift.

363
00:20:46,464 --> 00:20:47,464
Of course.

364
00:20:53,145 --> 00:20:54,881
Why are you out so early?

365
00:20:55,352 --> 00:20:56,999
Still dealing with jet lag?

366
00:20:57,297 --> 00:21:00,334
Yeah. I'm exhausted, but I can't sleep.

367
00:21:01,218 --> 00:21:03,030
Ji Hu got his memory back.

368
00:21:03,032 --> 00:21:04,327
Let's throw a party.

369
00:21:04,328 --> 00:21:05,451
What party?

370
00:21:05,565 --> 00:21:07,498
They'll be too busy dating now.

371
00:21:08,318 --> 00:21:12,007
Yesterday, I got a taste of what it's like
to be the third wheel.

372
00:21:12,265 --> 00:21:14,038
They went on a date right after meeting.

373
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:16,698
Are they dating already?

374
00:21:17,938 --> 00:21:19,429
I supported them, but...

375
00:21:19,754 --> 00:21:22,040
now that they're actually dating,
I'm a little jealous.

376
00:21:22,041 --> 00:21:24,627
- What? Are you jealous?
- Of course.

377
00:21:25,285 --> 00:21:27,380
I can't believe Ji Ni is dating before me.

378
00:21:33,092 --> 00:21:34,715
My aunt made it for me.

379
00:21:35,851 --> 00:21:37,780
She helped me so much this time.

380
00:21:38,607 --> 00:21:39,965
I'm so glad.

381
00:21:40,985 --> 00:21:44,425
It's so comforting
to have her by your side.

382
00:21:45,259 --> 00:21:46,259
Come on, eat.

383
00:21:47,898 --> 00:21:49,288
I'm already full just being here.

384
00:21:49,918 --> 00:21:54,642
I still can't believe I'm sitting here,
talking and eating with you.

385
00:21:55,921 --> 00:21:57,498
But does your head really feel clear now?

386
00:21:58,758 --> 00:22:01,772
I still blank out for a moment sometimes,
but they say it'll get better.

387
00:22:02,665 --> 00:22:04,770
Some people get their memories back
faster than I did,

388
00:22:04,874 --> 00:22:06,370
but usually it takes a long time.

389
00:22:06,556 --> 00:22:08,791
- I'm lucky.
- I'm so glad.

390
00:22:09,152 --> 00:22:10,843
I can't believe I'm finally lucky.

391
00:22:11,896 --> 00:22:13,155
I'm so grateful.

392
00:22:13,305 --> 00:22:16,085
So stop saying you're unlucky from now on.

393
00:22:22,752 --> 00:22:24,598
What are you going to do about Do Hee?

394
00:22:26,791 --> 00:22:28,018
I'll meet her today.

395
00:22:29,232 --> 00:22:31,433
So much happened while I had amnesia,

396
00:22:31,772 --> 00:22:33,299
and now it's hard to sort out.

397
00:22:34,252 --> 00:22:36,820
By the way, what's that?

398
00:22:37,328 --> 00:22:40,932
Why did my dad buy a dress from your mom?

399
00:22:41,831 --> 00:22:43,467
My dad wore a dress?

400
00:22:43,798 --> 00:22:45,138
That makes no sense.

401
00:22:48,412 --> 00:22:52,058
So quite a few of the puzzle pieces
are mixed up.

402
00:22:55,792 --> 00:22:58,212
Why are you laughing like an idiot
when you don't know anything?

403
00:22:58,272 --> 00:23:01,178
I'm smiling because you're smiling, Ji Ni.

404
00:23:02,172 --> 00:23:04,200
Because I'm your mirror, right?

405
00:23:06,798 --> 00:23:07,798
That's so cheesy.

406
00:23:08,118 --> 00:23:09,967
That's so cheesy.

407
00:23:11,355 --> 00:23:12,355
What's this?

408
00:23:12,981 --> 00:23:14,356
Come on, eat.

409
00:23:18,112 --> 00:23:19,471
- Is it good?
- Yeah.

410
00:23:19,959 --> 00:23:23,421
Do you know how hard it is for Ji Ni
to let herself love someone?

411
00:23:25,425 --> 00:23:26,888
Ji Hu is a good guy.

412
00:23:27,058 --> 00:23:28,838
Please, just reconsider.

413
00:23:29,092 --> 00:23:32,972
Even if she weren't your daughter,
would you watch her jump into a fire?

414
00:23:37,564 --> 00:23:39,671
What's the point of Ji Hu
being a good guy?

415
00:23:39,732 --> 00:23:41,458
Marriage involves the whole family.

416
00:23:41,831 --> 00:23:44,211
Do you want her to end up like me
by ignoring that?

417
00:23:44,678 --> 00:23:47,632
Yeong Ju, I've spent my whole life
in tears.

418
00:23:48,112 --> 00:23:50,443
Please, at least try to stop Ji Ni.

419
00:23:50,445 --> 00:23:51,676
She listens to you.

420
00:23:51,678 --> 00:23:54,112
Are they going to get married?
Move abroad?

421
00:23:54,772 --> 00:23:57,471
We only just found out how Ji Ni feels.
Don't do this.

422
00:23:57,498 --> 00:24:00,198
If it's the wrong path,
you have to stop her from the start.

423
00:24:00,738 --> 00:24:03,898
Ji Ni couldn't even go to high school
because of Do Hee.

424
00:24:04,171 --> 00:24:06,505
I hate this endless, twisted fate
between them.

425
00:24:06,872 --> 00:24:09,839
Why does it have to be the man
Do Hee is so obsessed with?

426
00:24:10,647 --> 00:24:11,647
It's ominous.

427
00:24:12,038 --> 00:24:13,038
Yeah.

428
00:24:13,517 --> 00:24:17,051
Yeong Ju, please. I'm begging you.

429
00:24:19,365 --> 00:24:20,365
Seriously...

430
00:24:21,078 --> 00:24:23,009
Is your daughter dating?

431
00:24:24,314 --> 00:24:26,445
Do Hee's ex-boyfriend?

432
00:24:27,758 --> 00:24:29,401
How did you find out?

433
00:24:30,678 --> 00:24:32,705
Right, that "Love in Zip" thing?

434
00:24:34,612 --> 00:24:36,408
Just pretend you didn't hear anything
for now.

435
00:24:36,410 --> 00:24:39,551
Of course. I'm on my artist's side.

436
00:24:41,578 --> 00:24:43,171
Take a look at this.

437
00:24:45,698 --> 00:24:47,979
If you're okay with it,
I guess it's all good.

438
00:24:56,098 --> 00:24:57,558
Ji Hu, why are we here?

439
00:24:58,948 --> 00:24:59,948
You know this place, right?

440
00:25:00,423 --> 00:25:02,678
Sure. Your dad's book storage room.

441
00:25:03,258 --> 00:25:06,174
I don't read, but there's something nice
about this place.

442
00:25:11,232 --> 00:25:13,010
You locked Ji Ni in here.

443
00:25:13,745 --> 00:25:15,772
We escaped from here
and ran for a long time.

444
00:25:16,132 --> 00:25:20,146
We encouraged each other to break free
from the things we felt trapped by.

445
00:25:20,585 --> 00:25:22,478
That's the drawing that was in my room.

446
00:25:22,512 --> 00:25:23,888
You didn't know anything about it,

447
00:25:25,269 --> 00:25:27,102
yet you lied and said you drew it.

448
00:25:28,489 --> 00:25:29,489
Ji Hu?

449
00:25:30,942 --> 00:25:32,252
I remember everything now.

450
00:25:32,765 --> 00:25:34,194
You hit me with your car.

451
00:25:34,654 --> 00:25:37,835
I collapsed, and Ji Ni prayed for me.

452
00:25:37,883 --> 00:25:38,971
You even...

453
00:25:39,812 --> 00:25:41,018
tried to marry me...

454
00:25:42,439 --> 00:25:43,983
when I had no memory.

455
00:25:43,984 --> 00:25:44,984
And...

456
00:25:46,285 --> 00:25:47,965
you planned to take me back to London.

457
00:25:51,288 --> 00:25:52,288
Ji Hu.

458
00:25:52,807 --> 00:25:53,807
Congratulations.

459
00:25:54,881 --> 00:25:55,966
You really mean that?

460
00:25:56,403 --> 00:25:57,403
Of course.

461
00:25:58,337 --> 00:25:59,445
Congratulations.

462
00:26:01,027 --> 00:26:02,027
Then,

463
00:26:04,258 --> 00:26:06,468
you remember how much I like you,

464
00:26:07,265 --> 00:26:08,736
don't you?

465
00:26:10,852 --> 00:26:12,508
Enough to kill Ji Ni,

466
00:26:13,049 --> 00:26:15,141
enough to want to die,

467
00:26:16,292 --> 00:26:19,911
and that I gave my whole heart
to no one but you.

468
00:26:19,945 --> 00:26:22,432
I told you clearly
the night before the accident.

469
00:26:23,705 --> 00:26:25,455
Even if Ji Ni rejected me,

470
00:26:26,509 --> 00:26:27,918
things between us were over.

471
00:26:29,018 --> 00:26:30,723
I told you to leave your parents too...

472
00:26:31,495 --> 00:26:33,011
and find the love that's right for you.

473
00:26:33,878 --> 00:26:34,878
Ji Hu.

474
00:26:35,662 --> 00:26:37,652
- That was so long ago.
- No.

475
00:26:38,058 --> 00:26:39,149
No matter when,

476
00:26:39,487 --> 00:26:42,271
even if I didn't regain my memories
for another 30 years,

477
00:26:43,076 --> 00:26:44,929
we'd have to start over from that point.

478
00:26:46,193 --> 00:26:49,528
- That's only fair.
- I didn't do this on my own.

479
00:26:50,545 --> 00:26:52,700
Your parents approved too.

480
00:26:53,918 --> 00:26:56,052
They hate Ji Ni because of her birth,

481
00:26:58,392 --> 00:26:59,657
but I'll take care of that.

482
00:27:00,185 --> 00:27:01,185
How?

483
00:27:02,319 --> 00:27:05,431
Can you change how Ji Ni was born?

484
00:27:05,432 --> 00:27:06,520
Let's talk about you.

485
00:27:09,858 --> 00:27:12,215
What about me?

486
00:27:12,329 --> 00:27:14,144
You're the only one I have.

487
00:27:14,618 --> 00:27:17,098
I could tell you a million times,
but why do you still...

488
00:27:18,824 --> 00:27:21,254
Why do you keep hurting me like this?

489
00:27:22,521 --> 00:27:24,011
I'm hurting too.

490
00:27:24,012 --> 00:27:25,992
I'm a woman too. This isn't fair.

491
00:27:27,405 --> 00:27:29,035
Why won't you accept my love?

492
00:27:31,418 --> 00:27:33,091
Why do you keep ignoring me?

493
00:27:38,665 --> 00:27:39,976
I never meant it, but...

494
00:27:41,569 --> 00:27:43,037
I'm sorry for breaking my promise.

495
00:27:43,891 --> 00:27:46,011
We can't go any further. Accept it.

496
00:27:46,458 --> 00:27:48,228
Even if I'm thrown out
and end up homeless,

497
00:27:49,462 --> 00:27:50,918
I won't marry just to survive.

498
00:28:19,427 --> 00:28:20,780
(Marriage Certificate)

499
00:28:20,782 --> 00:28:23,548
(Self, Do Do Hee, Spouse, Im Ji Hu)

500
00:28:50,185 --> 00:28:53,570
(Family Register)

501
00:28:53,572 --> 00:28:54,658
Is that a marriage certificate?

502
00:28:54,659 --> 00:28:55,803
Didn't you agree to this?

503
00:28:55,805 --> 00:28:57,819
Nothing can change now. Forget Ji Ni.

504
00:28:57,820 --> 00:28:59,682
You're selling me off to a murderer!

505
00:28:59,683 --> 00:29:01,633
- Im Ji Hu!
- Now Na Ji Ni is a mistress.

506
00:29:01,634 --> 00:29:03,590
- Just like her mom.
- You're not the only one with a knife.

507
00:29:03,591 --> 00:29:06,188
What is it about Na Ji Ni
that makes you go this far?

508
00:29:06,190 --> 00:29:07,755
- What?
- Now, legally,

509
00:29:07,757 --> 00:29:08,937
I can drag you around by your hair.

510
00:29:08,938 --> 00:29:11,423
How could you do this to my dear Ji Ni?

511
00:29:11,425 --> 00:29:12,612
I'm sorry, Ji Ni.

512
00:29:14,135 --> 00:29:16,135
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
